---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Spidergraph — Stuck Account Ledger"
  description="For accounts a service won't delete: generate plausible replacement details in your browser, and keep a record of what you changed, where and when, so you can still get back in."
  path="stuck-account-ledger/"
  current="stuck-ledger"
  accent="red"
>
  <link
    slot="head"
    rel="stylesheet"
    href={`${base}pages/stuck-account-ledger.css`}
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">
          Self-audit · <span id="itemCount">0</span> stuck accounts tracked
        </div>
        <h1>
          Stuck Account <span>Ledger</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="sub">
          Some services won't delete an account. When that happens, cut its
          links, overwrite what it still shows with made-up details, and keep a
          record here of what you changed. The details are generated in your
          browser, and everything stays in this browser.
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="reset-btn" id="resetBtn">
        Reset ledger
      </button>
    </header>

    <div class="intro-card">
      <b>Why the record matters:</b> once a profile holds made-up details, a
      password reset or a security question may ask for them back. Without a
      note of what you entered, overwriting can lock you out of an account you
      still need to close. Each account below follows the steps of
      <b>Runbook H</b> in the Playbook, and reminds you to check after 30 and 90
      days that the new details stuck.
      <div class="links">
        <a href="../playbook/#runbook-h-stuck-account-no-delete-option-deactivate-only-data-kept-after-deletion-or-other-services-still-sign-in-through-it">
          📖 Read Runbook H in the Playbook →
        </a>
        <a href="../playbook/#1-identity-account-foundation">
          📖 Email aliases: Domain 1 →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="layout">
      <div>
        <div class="list-head">
          <span class="list-head-title">Stuck accounts</span>
        </div>
        <form class="add-row" id="addForm">
          <input
            type="text"
            id="svcInput"
            placeholder="Service (e.g. an old forum)"
            aria-label="Service name"
            maxlength="80"
            required
          />
          <input
            type="url"
            id="urlInput"
            placeholder="https://… (optional)"
            aria-label="Account or settings page URL"
            maxlength="300"
          />
          <select id="outcomeInput" aria-label="What happened">
            <option value="no-delete">No delete option</option>
            <option value="deactivate">Deactivate only</option>
            <option value="retains">Keeps data after deleting</option>
            <option value="login-linked">
              Other services sign in through it
            </option>
            <option value="refused">Request refused</option>
          </select>
          <button type="submit" id="addBtn">
            Add account
          </button>
        </form>
        <div class="empty-state" id="emptyState">
          No stuck accounts yet. Add one above when a service won't let you
          delete your account.
        </div>
        <div id="acctList"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Progress</div>
          <div class="score-row">
            <div>
              <div class="score-num" id="scoreNum">
                0%
              </div>
              <div class="score-label">accounts handled and checked</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Steps done</span>
            <span class="v teal" id="mSteps">
              0/0
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Checks due</span>
            <span class="v amber" id="mDue">
              0
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Replacement details</div>
          <p class="small">
            Plausible values, made in this browser from built-in word lists.
            Phone numbers use 555-0100 to 555-0199, the range reserved for
            fiction, so they can't be someone's real number. There's no email
            field: keep an email you control on the account.
          </p>
          <dl class="gen-list" id="genList"></dl>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="reset-btn"
            id="genBtn"
            style="width:100%"
          >
            Generate new set
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Before you overwrite</div>
          <ul class="small">
            <li>
              Leave alone anything you still need to sign in or recover the
              account: its email, phone for codes, security key.
            </li>
            <li>
              Some services' terms forbid false details. Whether to overwrite
              there is your decision.
            </li>
            <li>
              A generated street address can match a real one by chance. Use it
              only where the service insists on an address.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Export</div>
          <p class="small">
            A text file of every account and the values you set. It holds no
            passwords; keep it with your other account records.
          </p>
          <button type="button" id="exportBtn" class="reset-btn">
            Export ledger ↓
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">History</div>
          <p class="small">
            Save a dated checkpoint to compare your progress over time.
          </p>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="snapshotBtn"
            class="reset-btn"
            style="width:100%; margin-bottom:12px;"
          >
            Save snapshot
          </button>
          <div id="historyList" class="history-list"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <b>Companion pages:</b> Runbook H in the <b>Playbook</b> explains each
      step; the <b>Broker Removal Tracker</b> covers people-search listings
      rather than your own accounts. Everything here stays in this browser, in
      <code>localStorage</code>: nothing is sent anywhere, and the replacement
      details are generated on this page, not fetched from a service.
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script src={`${base}shared/persist.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/history.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/decoy-generator.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}pages/stuck-account-ledger.js`} is:inline></script>
</BaseLayout>
